WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.620
- Now is a terrible, horrible,
no good, very bad time

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.547
to buy a car.

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:07.465
Sure, inflation is slowing down

00:00:07.465 --> 00:00:09.990
and supply chains are coming back online,

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.938
but now might be the worst
time ever to buy a car,

00:00:12.938 --> 00:00:14.880
especially a new car.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.710
There are three big reasons

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.720
that Americans who go
car shopping right now

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.140
are going to pay more and
get less for their money,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.680
high prices, high demand, poor selection.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.700
I'll explain.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.220
First, let's talk about those high costs.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.980
New car prices are sky high right now.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.740
Five years ago, there were
a dozen new car models

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.990
that sold for less than $20,000.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:39.007
In 2023, there's one.

00:00:39.007 --> 00:00:40.260
(car horn honking)

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.660
The Mitsubishi Mirage Hatchback.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.730
Whoo, swaging.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.188
It's true that new car
prices have been coming down

00:00:47.188 --> 00:00:48.745
since hitting record highs,

00:00:48.745 --> 00:00:52.260
but US Treasury yields recently
rose their highest level

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.090
in more than 15 years.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.820
We've seen a similar increase
in the rates for auto loans,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.670
and the cost of financing
a car hit an all time high

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.700
in the second quarter, so drivers
who financed their vehicle

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.460
are actually paying more
than when prices were higher.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.080
Car shopping website, Edmunds,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.450
found that a record 17% of customers

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.031
who financed were paying
more than $1,000 a month.

00:01:12.031 --> 00:01:13.620
(cash register dinging)

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.320
And then there's
insurance and maintenance.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.240
The latest CPI inflation report

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.690
showed motor vehicle
insurance costs rose by 19%

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:22.710
from a year ago.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.740
That was the largest increase
of all items in the report.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.600
And just below auto insurance

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.060
was the 12% increase in maintenance costs

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.980
for cars and trucks.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.897
- [Protesters] Corporate
greed has got to go.

00:01:33.897 --> 00:01:36.360
- Oh, and the United Auto
Workers recently announced

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.580
a strike at the big three automakers,

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.430
so car production could slow even further.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:45.750
The UAW is seeking a 46% pay
increase over four years,

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.760
so this fight could last a while.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.330
And once it's done, car
prices might just go up again.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:54.030
Car prices are being
held up by high demand,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.640
which means there's a lot
of people trying to buy.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.580
Production slowed down
significantly in recent years,

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.610
and that has left a shortage
of millions of new cars.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.920
People didn't just stop needing new cars,

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.810
because they weren't being produced,

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.920
so folks who couldn't buy
then are trying to buy now.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.980
That's creating something
of a feeding frenzy on lots.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.980
The latest inventory report
from Cox Automotive found

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.690
that while inventory has rebounded

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.480
from 2021 and 2022 levels,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.570
it has remained low by
historical standards.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.800
And we all know what happens

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.800
when there's high demand and low supply,

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.500
it's hard for prices
to come down very much.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.840
That lack of production
in recent years also means

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.490
that used cars are fewer and
older than in years past.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.220
51% of used cars sold
in the second quarter

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.200
were more than three years old.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.370
That's up from 42% before the
pandemic according to Edmunds.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.590
So what's it all mean?

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.407
It could mean that now's
a good time to invest

00:02:51.407 --> 00:02:55.260
in a nice bicycle or a bus pass.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.840
The latest CPI report
shows new vehicle prices

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.480
have fallen in three of
the last five months,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.430
and used car and truck prices have fallen

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.040
by more than 6.5% from last year.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.840
So you might wanna wait or
lower your standards a bit.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.710
Whatever you do, now is
definitely not a good time

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.826
to buy a new car.

00:03:14.826 --> 00:03:17.409
(upbeat music)

